`RiemannAlign` works on the covariance of each window's tokens, centered on their mean, instead of their second moments: tokens are not zero-mean, and for some models (LUNA) the mean token made up 97% of the matrix, so the tangent vectors described where the tokens sat rather than how they co-vary. A window needs at least two tokens that are not all the same; every matrix is then positive definite (shrinkage 0.1 toward the scaled identity).
